{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 16, :comments ["<b>And after.</b> After she returned to the camp, on the twenty-ninth of Sivan." "<b>And they encamped in the wilderness of Paran.</b> This is Kadesh Barnea. And this was how it unfolded: on the twentieth of Iyar they came from Chorev to the Graves of Craving, and it was not said 'consecrate yourselves for tomorrow' until the twenty-second of Iyar. Concerning this it is written: ״ויסעו מהר ה׳ דרך שלשת ימים״, so that I may bring you a reckoning: on the ninth of Av it was decreed upon our fathers that they would not enter the Land, and 'until a month of days' — 'until' and not 'until and including' — that makes the twenty-second of Sivan. And they ate the quail for seven days, from [the end of] Iyar until the twenty-second of Sivan. On that very day, the twenty-second of Sivan, they came to Hazeroth. On the morrow, the twenty-third, they prepared themselves to journey from Hazeroth, as explained. They tarried there until Miriam's gathering on the seventh day, which is the twenty-ninth of Sivan. On that very day they came to Kadesh Barnea and sent the spies, as is found in tractate Ta'anit. <b>The order of the portion of Beha'alotekha works out well.</b>"], :book :numbers, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 12, :notes {1 "The final line, שלימא סדרא דפרשת בהעלותך, is a concluding colophon ('the order/chronology of the parashah of Beha'alotekha works out well'), apparently validating the date calculation across the portion."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:17:45.950268244Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}